    "updated_at": "2025-05-20T08:20:28Z",
    "body": "This was attempted in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5749, but we got stuck. At this point the latest plan is for @syg to move structured cloning into the JavaScript specification, so that we stop missing things added to the ECMAScript types. Until that work happens, you can consider the set of properties cloned to be frozen to the set of properties that are in the JS spec as of ~2020. (So, Chromium and Firefox are actually not conformant to the current spec, which does not allow copying `cause`.)",
